  "articleSummary": "The article argues that AI agents are useless without integrations into business systems (e.g., Salesforce, Jira) and that the Model Context Protocol (MCP) solves the integration problem by providing a standardized USB-C-like interface. It explains how Mastra’s `MCPClient` allows agents to connect multiple tools (e.g., maps, weather, Wikipedia) without writing custom API wrappers, and addresses per-user authentication for production security. The tone is analytical and instructive, targeting developers who build agents and need practical integration patterns. The USB-C metaphor frames MCP as a universal connector that eliminates fragmented, custom integrations.",
